// A dangling FILE behind a USED alias. `2b4m check` prints
// "OK: 3 declarations, 0 theorems proven", exit 0 — "no-such-file.b4m" does not exist.
//
// Both landed checks correctly stay quiet: the IMPORT is mentioned (by the sort alias) and
// the ALIAS is used (by the const). Neither is a syntactic defect. Only RESOLUTION would
// catch this, and the demand-driven engine never resolves an alias nothing DEMANDS — a
// declaration with no proof above it is never demanded.
//
// NOTE the const is load-bearing for this repro: drop it and the 2026-10-21 unused-alias
// check fires instead, which is a different (and now-closed) defect.
import lib <<< "no-such-file.b4m"
sort A = lib.X
const Z: A
